A||N||12||Jefrysuko||Tires for 14" Hi-Tech rims||||1||
Z||000000||Jefrysuko||09-16-2001||09:55 PM||||Hello all,<BR>I am looking for some new tires for my 86 SE V6 and want opinions.  I am going to stick with the stock 14" Hi-Tech Aluminum Rims so that is what I have to work with.  This is my daily driven car so I need all-season performance and I also plan on doing a little autocrossing and drag-racing.  If I ever plan on doing a lot of racing I will get a set of dedicated tires but for now I need to be practical.<P>For size I am planning on running 215/60/R14.  I am wondering if anyone has run 205/front and 215/rear on the 14's.  If there is another size you like please let me know.<P>For tires I am thinking about BFGoodrich Comp BT/A HR4-2 for $55.  The price is right and I have lower performance Comp T/A's on another car and like them.<P>Thank you<BR>Jeffrey<P>Edit for spelling<BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jefrysuko (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||09-17-2001||11:21 AM||||Am I the only one still running 14" rims?  I know it isn't that popular but dosn't anyone have an opinion?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000002||Formula88||09-17-2001||11:40 AM||||For the money, the CompT/A's are hard to beat.  I've got Bridgestone Potenza RE950's on my Formula, but they're about $80-100 each, depending on size.  If you like the CompT/A's, I'd stay with them.  You won't find much better for your 14" rims.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||09-17-2001||03:11 PM||||Thanks Formula good to know someone is listening.<P>I am still wanting to see if someone has run the 205/front 215/rear combination on 14".  I am thinking that this might even out the wheel gap a little bit and give reduced steering effort while not compromising the handling much if at all.  Also the narrower tires will help the tendency of the front tires from turning into skis in the snow.<P>Hope someone has some thoughts on this.<P>Jeffrey<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||HummelHund||09-17-2001||06:04 PM||||I've got Yokohama Avid T4 215/60's on my 14" wheels and I am very pleased with their performance. Only cost $54 a tire, too. I'm sure Comp T/A's would be better, but I couldn't spend that much on tires.<BR>Sorry, I don't know of anyone with 205's on the front 14 inchers, but I've got a friend with a GT with 15" wheels on it with 205's in front.<BR>Wait a minute, I just re-read your first post. Comp T/A's for $50+? They were about $70 when I bought my Yokies from the Tire Rack. Grrr....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project/daily driver)<BR>'84 SE (Dad's Project)<p>[This message has been edited by HummelHund (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jncomutt||09-17-2001||06:18 PM||||I have 205/60 on the front of my car with the 14" tech rims.  I'm not sure of the brand off hand but they have an "aquatread"  type V groove throughout the foot of the tire.  They handle well but I'm still noticing a lot of "push" and understeer. I also have the car lowered only in the front.  Probably makes matters different too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jefrysuko||09-17-2001||07:22 PM||||Hummel: Yeah I think the Comp T/A's are a little better.  I might check on that.  The price that I posted was from Tire Rack also.  I think that I can get them for just over $60 installed at Sam's Club.<P>Jncomutt: I am a little worried about understeer also.  I am no driving expert so I don't know how my ideas will actually affect the car.  I actually just looked it up and I can't get the 205 in Comp T/A's.  I will have to go to Touring T/A's.  I wonder if having two different tires would affect anything.<P>Jeffrey<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||09-18-2001||07:48 AM||||I've been running the T/A's for years and think they are pretty a good value.  I've got an 85SE v-6 4spd with the stock 14" aluminum rims and stock size 205 70R14s.||||reg||1
Z||000008||heavyhorse||09-18-2001||09:05 AM||||I too am running the original 14 inch rims.  I prefer to keep as much original as possible.  My 86 SE originally came with Eagle GT's which are no longer made.  I am using Eagle GT II which is supposedly the replacement to the Eagle GT.  I love 'em.  They wear great and the car drives like it was originally designed to.  I tried Eagle GT + 4 when they made them, but they didn't wear well, cost more, and I wasn't impressed with the ride.||||reg||1
Z||000009||heavyhorse||09-18-2001||09:06 AM||||by they way, they are 215/60's on all four corners||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jefrysuko||09-18-2001||01:54 PM||||Carrolles: Yeah I don't think I have ever found anyone that has been disatisfied with B/F Goodwrench tires.  I have personally put them on every car that has needed tires.  Just for your info though they make more than one line with the T/A designation.  Comp T/A, Radial T/A, Touring T/A etc.  Also they make different versions within those destinctions which is mainly speed ratings.  Also your size is not a stock size.  195/70R14 and 215/60R14 are the only two sizes that were put on 14" rims from the factory.  Since you are running 205/70 I would believe that you probably have Radial T/A's or Control T/A's.  There is nothing wrong with you running those tires, except for your spedometer being off a little bit, I just thought I would let you know.<P>Horse: Yeah I am running Eagle GT II on my 88 GT because the previous owner wanted to keep it stock as possible also.  I like your statement "They wear great and the car drives like it was originally designed to."  The truth of the matter is I am trying to get the car to perform "better" than it was originally designed to.  The Comp T/A's are rated as a "High Performance" tire where as the Eagles are only "Performance" tires.  I have read a few reports and the Comp T/A's have the numbers to back it up also.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||MrPBody||09-18-2001||10:13 PM||||I just got Viper 195/65 for the front, from NTB.  I have not yet replaced the rear, which are 215/60.  Feels good so far, but I haven't tried to flog it yet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jefrysuko||09-18-2001||10:21 PM||||Let me know what you think after you have had a chance to test it out.  I actually have a set of 195/70 that I could keep on the front but they are just a little bit taller than 215/60 and am afraid that would make it look weird.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrPBody:<BR><B>I just got Viper 195/65 for the front, from NTB.  I have not yet replaced the rear, which are 215/60.  Feels good so far, but I haven't tried to flog it yet.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
